You think of the spyglass, a gift from Cyrus. Standing on the upland, with the path leading to the lowland, perhaps using the spyglass will help you find a more convenient route? You don't want to force your way through the thicket again or trudge through tall plants.

The spyglass is old but still serves its purpose. You adjust the focus and survey the surroundings, imagining yourself as a pirate captain. It seems there's not only a direct path to the water, but also a detour. You can simply follow the edge of the forest you just emerged from. As far as you can see, there are no obstacles, and it's not as hot there as in the open ground.

It's a long walk, but you're confident that this decision is the right one. After some time, you step onto the silty lakeside.